        "id": 1110619
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-09-25T00:40:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "motion sensor code only init the device 1 time on power on.\n\nAfter the default initialization, a linux upper layer application can call set_data_rate with any value at any time.   \n\nIf power cycle is triggered, the sensor device will be re-initialized .  Then, the upper layer application need re-configure the data rate accordingly.  If upper layer application does not re-configure the date rate, then they use the default data rate, 119K.",
      "parentUuid": "f08beba0_89d7bcd0",
      "revId": "7d40063d46aa9a8b6146355ee9be9db775af7f0d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
